  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2014_che_a6.png\">\r\n\r\nThe longest chain contains 7 C-atom, so the root word is hept and suffix -ene is added for double bond along with its position. Since, two methyl goups are also present at 5 and 6 positions, so the correct IUPAC name of the compound is 5.6 -dimethylhept-2-ene.",
